{"name":"Japanese Iris","hex":"#7f5d3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"japanese iris","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A group of iris flower species native to or cultivated in East Asia, particularly in Japan, Korea, China, Russia, and Mongolia. Scientifically, the three primary species are Iris ensata, Iris laevigata, and Iris sanguinea."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fringed iris, of the species Iris japonica, native to China and Japan, not considered a Japanese iris species."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/japanese_iris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Japanese iris","blocks":[{"text":"The term \"Japanese iris\" encompasses three species of Irises cultivated in gardens or growing wild in Japan: hanashōbu, kakitsubata and ayame. Of these three species, I. ensata is the one most commonly referred to as \"Japanese iris\" outside Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Meigetuin02.jpg/330px-Meigetuin02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_iris","wikidata":"Q16753983"},{"title":"Iris (Japanese group)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is a Japanese idol girl group, formed in 2012 by Avex and 81 Produce. The group currently consists of five members: Saki Yamakita, Yū Serizawa, Himika Akaneya, Yuki Wakai, and Miyu Kubota. The leader is Saki Yamakita. In addition to their music career, all members are also active as voice actresses, most notably in the video game and anime series PriPara. The group has also performed themes for the anime series Wise Man's Grandchild, Magical Girl Site, Magical Sempai, and Twin Star Exorcists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(Japanese_group)","wikidata":"Q11224956"},{"title":"Iris (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is a flowering plant genus of 320 accepted species with showy flowers. As well as being the scientific name, iris is also widely used as a common name for all Iris species, as well as some belonging to other closely related genera. A common name for some species is flags, while the plants of the subgenus Scorpiris are widely known as junos, particularly in horticulture. It is a popular garden flower."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(plant)","wikidata":"Q156901"},{"title":"Iris (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is an ambiguous color term, usually referring to shades ranging from blue-violet to violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg/330px-Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(color)","wikidata":"Q6070109"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Iris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg/500px-Iris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Iris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg/1280px-Iris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Iris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg/500px-Iris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iris ensata (including Iris kaempferi)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIris_ensata_var_ensata2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/%E3%80%90%E6%9C%AC%E4%BA%88%E5%91%8A%E3%80%91%E5%8A%87%E5%A0%B4%E7%89%88%E3%82%A2%E3%83%8B%E3%83%A1%E3%80%8Ci%E2%98%86Ris_the_Movie_-_Full_Energy%21%21_-%E3%80%